{
  "id": "roots.contra-anti",
  "slug": "contra-anti",
  "ladder": "vocab",
  "course": "roots",
  "unit": "together-against",
  "title": "Against: contra-, anti- and ob-",
  "short": "contra-, counter-, anti- and ob- all carry the idea of against.",
  "trouble": "anti- (against) is not ante- (before). ob- hides in shapes like oc-, of- and op- (occur, offer, oppose).",
  "prereqs": [
    "roots.con-syn"
  ],
  "xp": 1,
  "viz": [
    "vo-roots",
    "vo-word"
  ],
  "figureArchetype": "GeneralFigure",
  "lesson": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "To <i>contradict</i> is to speak against, an <i>antidote</i> works against a poison and an <i>obstacle</i> stands in your way. Three prefixes carry the idea of “against”: Latin <b>contra-</b> (also <b>contro-</b> and <b>counter-</b>), Greek <b>anti-</b> and Latin <b>ob-</b>."
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-scene",
        "opts": {
          "scene": {
            "bg": "mountains",
            "cast": [
              {
                "who": "omar",
                "x": 30,
                "pose": "push",
                "mood": "determined",
                "face": "right",
                "wear": [
                  "backpack"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "props": [
              {
                "kind": "boulder",
                "x": 56,
                "s": 1.3
              },
              {
                "kind": "signpost",
                "x": 86,
                "s": 0.9,
                "text": "TOP"
              }
            ],
            "fx": [
              {
                "kind": "sweat",
                "on": "c0",
                "at": "head"
              }
            ],
            "labels": [
              {
                "text": "OB-STRUCT: in the way",
                "x": 50,
                "y": 92
              }
            ],
            "alt": "A hiker pushes against a big boulder blocking the trail."
          }
        },
        "cap": "A hiker pushes against a big boulder blocking the trail."
      },
      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "<b>contra-</b>, <b>contro-</b>, <b>counter-</b> = <b>against</b>. <b>anti-</b> (Greek) = <b>against, opposite</b>. <b>ob-</b> = <b>against, in the way</b>, and sometimes <b>toward</b>."
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "<b>ob-</b> hides in many shapes: <b>oc-</b> (<i>occur</i>), <b>of-</b> (<i>offend</i>), <b>op-</b> (<i>oppose</i>). The list’s <i>ob-</i> words are mostly about stubbornness and blocking: <i>obstinate</i>, <i>obdurate</i>, <i>obstruct</i>. In <i>obsequious</i>, though, <i>ob-</i> means “toward”: following toward someone, too eager to please."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "The parts and their words"
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "roots": [
            "contra",
            "anti"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "contra- and anti- (against)."
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "root": "ob"
        },
        "cap": "Words on the list built on ob- (against, in the way)."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "Words taken apart"
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Word and meaning",
          "Parts, and what they say"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "<b>controversy</b><br>a long public disagreement",
            "<b>contro-</b> <i>against</i> + vers <i>turn</i> + -y<br>→ “a turning against”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>counterfeit</b><br>made to look real in order to deceive",
            "<b>counter-</b> <i>in imitation of</i> + feit <i>made</i><br>→ “made as a copy”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>antithesis</b><br>the direct opposite",
            "<b>anti-</b> <i>against</i> + thesis <i>setting</i><br>→ “a setting against”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>antipathy</b><br>a strong dislike",
            "<b>anti-</b> <i>against</i> + path <i>feeling</i> + -y<br>→ “a feeling against”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>obstruct</b><br>to block",
            "<b>ob-</b> <i>in the way</i> + struct <i>build</i><br>→ “build in the way”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>obdurate</b><br>stubbornly refusing to change, especially when one should",
            "<b>ob-</b> <i>against</i> + dur <i>hard</i> + -ate<br>→ “hardened against”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>obsequious</b><br>too eager to please or obey",
            "<b>ob-</b> <i>toward</i> + sequ <i>follow</i> + -ious<br>→ “following toward (too eagerly)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b><i>antidote</i></b><br>a remedy that works against a poison",
            "<b>anti-</b> <i>against</i> + dote <i>given</i><br>→ “given against”"
          ]
        ],
        "cap": "Each word, what it means now, and its parts. Words in italics are familiar words that are not on the list."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Use the parts",
        "q": "The video of the play made the referee’s call <b>incontrovertible</b>. What does <i>incontrovertible</i> mean?",
        "steps": [
          "Take it apart: <b>in-</b> (not) + <b>contro-</b> (against) + <b>vert</b> (turn) + <b>-ible</b> (able to be).",
          "Literally: “not able to be turned against,” no one can argue the other way.",
          "The sentence fits: the video settled it."
        ],
        "a": "Beyond dispute."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "Meet the word",
        "card": true
      },
      {
