        "cap": "A word from the list: antipathy.",
        "card": true
      },
      {
        "t": "mistake",
        "html": "Mixing up <b>anti-</b> (against) and <b>ante-</b> (before). An <i>antidote</i> works against a poison; an <i>antecedent</i> comes before. Also watch for <b>ob-</b> in disguise: <i>oc-</i>, <i>of-</i> and <i>op-</i> (<i>occur</i>, <i>offer</i>, <i>oppose</i>)."
      },
      {
        "t": "note",
        "html": "In <b>counterfeit</b>, <i>counter-</i> carries the idea of “set against” as a match or copy: a counterfeit coin is made to stand against the real one and pass for it."
      },
      {
        "t": "try"
      }
